1
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:10,730
Sorry, Robbie. Sorry to be late this morning,

2
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:14,200
but, well, we've still got some time for a cup of coffee.

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,580
I can't wait to see my old pal Charley Rafer.

4
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:30,860
Neither can I.

5
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:32,590
So you thought about it, huh?

6
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:34,460
Yes, I have, Dad.

7
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,290
Well, I'm glad.

8
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:36,700
I knew you'd realize

9
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,580
that this interview could be an important experience for you.

10
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:42,410
I came to that conclusion.

11
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:44,850
That's very wise, Robbie.

12
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:47,420
Very wise.

13
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:50,960
Now let's head off for the city and the university club.

14
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,470
Thanks, Dad.

15
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:54,600
Thanks ... for what?

16
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,160
Thanks for hearing me out. And ...

17
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:58,650
And ...?

18
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:01,560
And thanks for being such an understanding father.

19
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:18,810
Well, thank you, Robbie. Thank you.

20
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:20,350
Philip Stewart!

21
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:21,640
It's great to see you!

22
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:29,230
Charley Rafer--you look as young as ever.

23
00:01:29,230 --> 00:01:30,470
You must be Robbie.

24
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:32,280
Hi.

25
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:35,120
Yes, this is my youngest son Robbie.

26
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,560
Robbie, I want you to meet

27
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:40,370
one of the best tennis players on the Michigan team--

28
00:01:40,370 --> 00:01:41,260
Charley Rafer.

29
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:42,750
Nice to meet you, Dean Rafer.

30
00:01:42,750 --> 00:01:45,740
Well, are you as good a tennis player as your dad?

31
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:48,410
No, I'm not very good at it.

32
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:50,630
Frankly, neither was I.

33
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:53,240
Charley was the star of the team.

34
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,820
Yeah. Thanks.

35
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,570
Well, how're you been, Philip?

36
00:01:56,570 --> 00:01:59,040
Oh, working too hard.

37
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,320
Doesn't show.

38
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:01,460
How's Ellen?

39
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,880
Fine, thank you.

40
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,850
And how's Marge?

41
00:02:05,850 --> 00:02:08,900
She's still giving the toughest English history exams

42
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:13,060
in the school and loving every minute of it.

43
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,480
And speaking of minutes,

44
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,340
I have interviews until noon,

45
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:19,470
so why don't we get right to work?

46
00:02:19,470 --> 00:02:21,730
Can you have lunch with us later?

47
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:23,600
I'd love to, Philip, but I'm afraid I can't.

48
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,910
I'm only here two days,

49
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:27,760
and I have interviews with twenty-six applicants.

50
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,970
I understand.

51
00:02:28,970 --> 00:02:30,230
Well, thanks.

52
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:33,650
I'll wait outside.

53
00:02:33,650 --> 00:02:35,670
Good luck, Son.

54
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:37,230
Did you bring your transcript from high school?

55
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:37,920
Yes, sir.

56
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:38,840
Right here.

57
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:41,320
Thank you.

58
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:47,480
Please sit down.

59
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,640
I see under "activities" that

60
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,430
you've been writing for the school paper.

61
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:52,320
Yes, sir.

62
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:54,030
What kinds of articles have you written?

63
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:58,780
All kinds--sports, editorials, theater reviews.

64
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:00,470
You name it, I've written it.

65
00:03:00,470 --> 00:03:02,150
Hmmm.

66
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:04,580
Well, have you ever thought of becoming a journalist?

67
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:06,590
A professional writer?

68
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:09,070
Not until recently.

69
00:03:09,070 --> 00:03:11,790
Michigan has a fine School of Journalism.

70
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:15,130
Yes, I know that.

71
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:17,580
You seem to have some reservations.

72
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:21,700
I'm a little uncertain.

73
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:23,440
It's been very nice talking to you.

74
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:26,220
Nice talking to you, sir.

75
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,910
One piece of advice.

76
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:33,360
The most important thing is for you to decide your own future.

77
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,180
Yes, sir.

78
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:36,270
Good-bye, Dean Rafer.

79
00:03:36,270 --> 00:03:39,270
Good-bye, Robbie. Good luck.
